1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,128
I also want to join you in this project.

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:05,905
Is your dream exclusive
only for the two of you?

3
00:00:05,905 --> 00:00:08,341
Of course not. You're part of my dreams, too.

4
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:10,217
Your boyfriend is handsome.

5
00:00:10,217 --> 00:00:12,070
Auntie, this is Hans.

6
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:13,211
My friend.

7
00:00:13,211 --> 00:00:14,899
You two look good together.

8
00:00:14,899 --> 00:00:18,233
- Liam, your family owns Casa Fuerte, right?
- Yes.

9
00:00:18,234 --> 00:00:20,567
An accident happened
at your construction site.

10
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:23,033
I should kill people like you.

11
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:25,234
I am surrounded by useless men!

12
00:00:25,234 --> 00:00:27,524
Spare me, Ramon. I'm a newbie.

13
00:00:27,524 --> 00:00:28,813
This is Lando.

14
00:00:28,813 --> 00:00:31,130
My most trusted gunman.

15
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:35,370
That face is the last thing you'll see
if you fail again, Danilo.

16
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:36,705
It's not too late yet.

17
00:00:36,705 --> 00:00:38,273
We can still break free
from Congressman Ramon.

18
00:00:38,273 --> 00:00:41,143
I know I wasn't the best father
for you and your brother.

19
00:00:41,143 --> 00:00:47,649
But someday, you'll understand
that I became a father the way I know how.

20
00:00:47,649 --> 00:00:49,351
I felt like I was dreaming.

21
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:51,620
I saw Joyce and Sep.

22
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,690
You and Joyce are husband and wife.

23
00:00:54,690 --> 00:00:57,392
You're a family.

24
00:00:57,392 --> 00:00:59,728
My husband became disabled
because of the incident,

25
00:00:59,728 --> 00:01:01,730
but I'm not just after the money.

26
00:01:01,730 --> 00:01:02,840
I want justice.

27
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,534
What will you do with justice
if it brings you trouble?

28
00:01:05,534 --> 00:01:08,604
Maybe I should come back some other day.

29
00:01:08,604 --> 00:01:11,706
Just call me when you're ready to talk.

30
00:01:22,618 --> 00:01:24,953
This place is so beautiful.

31
00:01:24,953 --> 00:01:27,144
But it's so chilly.

32
00:01:27,144 --> 00:01:28,390
I know.

33
00:01:28,390 --> 00:01:30,893
I should have brought my baby with me.

34
00:01:30,893 --> 00:01:31,960
Hey, hey, hey.

35
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:34,800
We're here for work, not for vacation.

36
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,833
That's not fun. It isn't lovely.

37
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:41,002
My OOTD is all set.

38
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:46,842
Director Phil, thank you so much
for staying with us.

39
00:01:46,842 --> 00:01:51,580
At my age, it isn't just about money anymore.

40
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:57,319
I will do it if the script is good, relevant,
and fights for something.

41
00:01:57,319 --> 00:01:58,420
Thank you so much.

42
00:01:58,420 --> 00:01:59,855
Yes.

43
00:01:59,855 --> 00:02:01,390
This is it, Liam.

44
00:02:02,991 --> 00:02:04,826
We can do this.

45
00:02:04,826 --> 00:02:06,465
Guys!

46
00:02:07,512 --> 00:02:09,376
- Liam.
- Mayor, how are you?

47
00:02:09,376 --> 00:02:13,502
Joyce. Director Phil, everyone,
welcome back to my private resort.

48
00:02:13,502 --> 00:02:17,339
I hope your filming will be smooth sailing.

49
00:02:17,339 --> 00:02:21,343
Mayor, thank you for letting us
film here again.

50
00:02:21,343 --> 00:02:22,911
Of course.

51
00:02:22,911 --> 00:02:25,580
I can't say no to Via.

52
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,916
Wow, I'm amazed by the connections.

53
00:02:27,916 --> 00:02:32,387
But I hope our connections
are clean and honest

54
00:02:32,387 --> 00:02:36,758
so that everybody's happy.

55
00:02:36,758 --> 00:02:38,593
And speaking of Via.

56
00:02:38,593 --> 00:02:40,083
Via!

57
00:02:41,029 --> 00:02:43,432
Mayor.

58
00:02:43,432 --> 00:02:46,868
Good evening. You look lovely.

59
00:02:46,868 --> 00:02:48,637
We're so sorry we're late.

60
00:02:48,637 --> 00:02:52,874
It took a long time
to pull out the other wardrobes.

61
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:56,778
Why do you look so surprised?

62
00:02:56,778 --> 00:03:00,414
I thought you were just going
to send the clothes.

63
00:03:01,841 --> 00:03:04,453
Are you saying you don't need me here?

64
00:03:04,453 --> 00:03:07,021
No, that's not what I meant.

65
00:03:07,956 --> 00:03:12,160
I can't leave you alone.

66
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,629
You already know, right? I told you.

67
00:03:14,629 --> 00:03:18,500
I'll give my all-out support
for your dream project with Joyce.

68
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,634
Mayor!

69
00:03:19,634 --> 00:03:23,672
Thank you so much for letting us film here.

70
00:03:23,672 --> 00:03:26,141
Via, seriously.

71
00:03:26,141 --> 00:03:28,477
You're always welcome.

72
00:03:28,477 --> 00:03:30,479
My house is your house.

73
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:31,980
Thank you.

74
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:35,684
I see you've met my boyfriend, Liam?

75
00:03:35,684 --> 00:03:38,786
He's the creative manager for our movie.

76
00:03:39,421 --> 00:03:42,457
Oh, and of course, Joyce.

77
00:03:42,457 --> 00:03:43,625
Of course!

78
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:46,094
Who doesn't know Joyce?

79
00:03:46,094 --> 00:03:49,325
But between you and me, I like Savana more.

80
00:03:49,325 --> 00:03:51,208
But then again...

81
00:03:51,208 --> 00:03:56,304
Via's friends are also my friends.

82
00:03:56,304 --> 00:04:00,809
I owe the dela Peñas a lot,
especially Congressman Ramon.

83
00:04:00,809 --> 00:04:04,279
So when I heard Via was part of this project,

84
00:04:04,279 --> 00:04:09,051
I let you use my private resort
as your location.

85
00:04:09,051 --> 00:04:10,952
Thank you so much, Mayor.

86
00:04:10,952 --> 00:04:13,355
But I'm sure everyone's
tired from the trip...

87
00:04:13,355 --> 00:04:16,224
Because I am tired, so...

88
00:04:16,224 --> 00:04:17,359
Of course.

89
00:04:17,359 --> 00:04:20,162
And everybody's feeling cold.

90
00:04:20,162 --> 00:04:23,165
I will bring you to your accommodations.

91
00:04:23,165 --> 00:04:24,766
Director Phil!

92
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,047
Love.

93
00:04:35,911 --> 00:04:37,316
Love...

94
00:04:38,267 --> 00:04:40,368
Did I hear it right?

95
00:04:41,732 --> 00:04:47,023
We got this location
because of your dad's connection to the Mayor?

96
00:04:47,025 --> 00:04:51,393
Honestly, love, I didn't know
that's what his consideration was.

97
00:04:51,393 --> 00:04:55,132
I'm sure he liked your script.

98
00:04:55,133 --> 00:05:00,468
Yeah, but I want to be really independent.

99
00:05:02,104 --> 00:05:04,838
I know you love your dad.

100
00:05:04,838 --> 00:05:08,415
But you saw what he could do, right?

101
00:05:08,415 --> 00:05:09,875
Love...

102
00:05:10,946 --> 00:05:12,980
Don't worry.

103
00:05:14,049 --> 00:05:17,252
As long as I'm with you...

104
00:05:17,252 --> 00:05:19,654
he won't touch you.

105
00:05:21,923 --> 00:05:23,454
I hope so.

106
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:28,095
I hope he really did let me go.

107
00:05:29,231 --> 00:05:32,332
Because I don't want anyone else
to get involved.

108
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:46,495
Is there a problem, Miss Via?

109
00:05:49,995 --> 00:05:53,657
Nothing I can't handle, Queenie.

110
00:05:54,756 --> 00:05:56,433
Okay.

111
00:06:54,449 --> 00:06:55,717
<i>The Congressman sent me...</i>

112
00:06:55,717 --> 00:06:56,851
<i>He has Big bro's blessing.</i>

113
00:06:56,851 --> 00:06:57,886
<i>Make sure of that.</i>

114
00:06:57,886 --> 00:07:00,403
<i>We don't want the chief to get in trouble.</i>

115
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:10,747
<i>Boss, I'm begging you.</i>

116
00:07:50,256 --> 00:07:52,558
You didn't fail me.

117
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:58,546
This is where our choices brought us.

118
00:08:02,549 --> 00:08:05,051
All we can do now is...

119
00:08:08,945 --> 00:08:11,913
deal with it together.

120
00:08:29,243 --> 00:08:31,978
Do you regret it?

121
00:08:36,584 --> 00:08:40,087
Do you regret being my husband?

122
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:47,761
If there's something I regret,
it is not being strong enough.

123
00:08:48,867 --> 00:08:55,139
I know I made mistakes
that I cannot rectify anymore.

124
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:02,644
Sir Liam's script is so good.

125
00:09:02,644 --> 00:09:04,812
It's so heartfelt.

126
00:09:06,915 --> 00:09:09,818
It's so deep.

127
00:09:09,818 --> 00:09:12,153
Well, it shows.

128
00:09:12,153 --> 00:09:15,657
It shows that he is so in love.

129
00:09:15,657 --> 00:09:17,992
That's why he is so inspired to write.

130
00:09:20,528 --> 00:09:22,329
But, thank you.

131
00:09:23,865 --> 00:09:26,600
Thank you for giving this another chance.

132
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:31,505
We will make everything right.

133
00:09:33,108 --> 00:09:35,543
Love is really something.

134
00:09:35,543 --> 00:09:39,013
Love can move mountains.

135
00:09:39,013 --> 00:09:43,017
But Sir Liam's script... his love...

136
00:09:43,017 --> 00:09:46,020
It feels like it can move
even the longest mountain range.

137
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:48,022
You're so weird.

138
00:09:48,022 --> 00:09:51,860
I wish he was inspired by Miss Via.

139
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:54,627
What do you mean, Queenie?

140
00:09:54,627 --> 00:09:57,627
Well, without question, your boss is in love.

141
00:09:57,627 --> 00:10:00,201
But the question is, who is he in love with?

142
00:10:00,201 --> 00:10:03,538
Oh my, oh my.

143
00:10:03,538 --> 00:10:07,709
Our country never progresses
because of issues like that.

144
00:10:07,709 --> 00:10:08,810
You really are an evil queen.

145
00:10:08,810 --> 00:10:16,084
I believe that my Boss Bro
is just following his heart.

146
00:10:16,084 --> 00:10:18,386
If I were Sir Liam,

147
00:10:18,386 --> 00:10:24,159
I would be with the person
who brings me real joy.

148
00:10:24,159 --> 00:10:26,766
I mean, happiness.

149
00:10:28,229 --> 00:10:32,066
Not all love stories have happy endings.

150
00:10:32,066 --> 00:10:36,498
Remember, don't mess with us, evil queens.

151
00:10:38,206 --> 00:10:41,976
Why don't you go in front of the camera?

152
00:10:43,805 --> 00:10:46,847
- It's your fault.
- You were so loud.

153
00:10:47,682 --> 00:10:48,850
Cut!

154
00:10:48,850 --> 00:10:50,001
Good take!

155
00:10:50,001 --> 00:10:51,085
Perfect!

156
00:10:51,085 --> 00:10:52,387
Lovely.

157
00:10:52,387 --> 00:10:56,424
Go call Miss Emmy and Mister Oscar.

158
00:10:56,424 --> 00:10:58,426
This is it, Lord!

159
00:11:00,527 --> 00:11:02,662
Miss Emmy...

160
00:11:07,402 --> 00:11:08,770
Joyce!

161
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:09,971
Joyce.

162
00:11:09,971 --> 00:11:11,454
Wait.

163
00:11:12,774 --> 00:11:13,908
Why?

164
00:11:13,908 --> 00:11:16,277
Aren't we done yet?

165
00:11:16,277 --> 00:11:19,447
Why? Is what you did not perfect?

166
00:11:21,616 --> 00:11:23,918
Liam...

167
00:11:23,918 --> 00:11:27,121
You don't have to flatter me.

168
00:11:27,121 --> 00:11:29,958
You already have me.

169
00:11:29,958 --> 00:11:31,459
What?

170
00:11:31,459 --> 00:11:34,418
For the film.

171
00:11:38,299 --> 00:11:42,303
I don't want this filming to end.

172
00:11:42,303 --> 00:11:50,178
It feels good to do what you love.

173
00:11:50,178 --> 00:11:53,113
And you're working with the people you like.

174
00:11:55,016 --> 00:12:00,054
This is the first time...

175
00:12:01,456 --> 00:12:06,627
that I've worked without stress.

176
00:12:08,299 --> 00:12:10,931
It feels strange.

177
00:12:12,976 --> 00:12:15,211
You know the feeling of...

178
00:12:16,697 --> 00:12:21,000
wanting to stop time...

179
00:12:23,311 --> 00:12:25,346
even for a short while.

180
00:12:26,681 --> 00:12:29,249
When you don't have problems...

181
00:12:30,852 --> 00:12:32,954
Everything is all right.

182
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:52,974
If only we could stay brave all the time...

183
00:12:52,974 --> 00:12:58,553
to fight against time.

184
00:12:58,553 --> 00:13:01,670
To go against the flow.

185
00:13:03,551 --> 00:13:06,653
Nothing is impossible if we want it, right?

186
00:13:13,595 --> 00:13:22,153
If only there is magic in our time.

187
00:13:26,841 --> 00:13:28,842
What if there is?

188
00:13:32,733 --> 00:13:36,017
Come on, Liam.

189
00:13:36,017 --> 00:13:40,754
We're too old to believe in magic.

190
00:13:44,759 --> 00:13:46,994
There's no such thing.

191
00:13:54,969 --> 00:13:57,371
But what if there really is magic?

192
00:14:13,203 --> 00:14:15,204
It's beautiful.

193
00:14:31,342 --> 00:14:33,540
Like a film.

194
00:14:34,509 --> 00:14:37,083
These things we see...

195
00:14:37,912 --> 00:14:41,114
That's what real magic is for me.

196
00:14:47,822 --> 00:14:53,996
But what if... there really is magic?

197
00:15:01,701 --> 00:15:03,550
I really hope so.

198
00:15:11,713 --> 00:15:13,647
What do you hope for?

199
00:15:23,391 --> 00:15:25,496
I really hope we can stop time...

200
00:15:28,086 --> 00:15:32,499
at the point in our lives
when we are worry-free.

201
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:42,410
<i>But let's admit that
even the best film has an ending.</i>

202
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:46,847
<i>Not all can be done with magic.</i>

203
00:16:13,853 --> 00:16:16,121
Siloy!

204
00:16:30,674 --> 00:16:32,675
What the!

205
00:16:40,321 --> 00:16:42,118
You really are tough.

206
00:16:44,272 --> 00:16:48,109
Edmond, I will repeat.

207
00:16:48,109 --> 00:16:51,578
Where's the money?

208
00:16:52,725 --> 00:16:55,827
I don't know what you're talking about.

209
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:06,594
<i>It's so loud!</i>

210
00:17:06,594 --> 00:17:09,063
<i>Are you going to tell us the truth?</i>

211
00:17:09,063 --> 00:17:13,835
Or should I bring your young daughter here?

212
00:17:13,835 --> 00:17:17,349
Leave my daughter out of this!

213
00:17:22,410 --> 00:17:24,411
What?

214
00:17:27,077 --> 00:17:28,649
<i>Aren't you going to tell us?</i>

215
00:17:28,649 --> 00:17:29,984
<i>Where is it?</i>

216
00:17:29,984 --> 00:17:32,918
It's gone!

217
00:17:32,918 --> 00:17:35,656
<i>It's me.</i>

218
00:17:37,625 --> 00:17:40,459
Mister Siloy doesn't want to talk yet.

219
00:17:40,459 --> 00:17:43,514
Yes, but I will go there and ask him. Okay?

220
00:17:43,514 --> 00:17:45,569
Okay, thank you.

221
00:17:46,944 --> 00:17:51,305
Bro, make sure they will be there later,
okay?

222
00:17:51,305 --> 00:17:52,640
Sir.

223
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:57,007
Siloy's wife said
she'd meet you at the morgue.

224
00:17:59,011 --> 00:18:00,475
Morgue?

225
00:18:00,475 --> 00:18:02,803
Siloy is already dead.

226
00:18:04,077 --> 00:18:05,457
What?

227
00:18:28,843 --> 00:18:32,146
These things we see...

228
00:18:32,146 --> 00:18:35,382
That's what real magic is for me.

229
00:18:42,823 --> 00:18:45,025
The film is complete.

230
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:54,668
Back to reality.

231
00:19:09,617 --> 00:19:11,507
Mom?

232
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:18,348
What's going on?

233
00:19:19,961 --> 00:19:21,796
Mom, hello?

234
00:19:21,796 --> 00:19:24,231
Mommy, what happened to Dad?

235
00:19:37,244 --> 00:19:40,448
I don't understand
what your father is thinking!

236
00:19:40,448 --> 00:19:43,784
- I thought he had changed!
- Auntie, Auntie.

237
00:19:43,784 --> 00:19:46,316
Calm down. I'm sorry.

238
00:19:46,316 --> 00:19:48,306
What happened?

239
00:19:51,134 --> 00:19:52,885
Dad...

240
00:19:58,447 --> 00:19:59,908
Joyce...

241
00:20:03,904 --> 00:20:06,039
Please forgive me.

242
00:20:17,785 --> 00:20:19,920
I thought you quit already?

243
00:20:32,230 --> 00:20:34,488
I'm sorry, my dear.

244
00:20:41,008 --> 00:20:43,577
It's okay, Dad.

245
00:20:45,279 --> 00:20:50,083
What matters is you're safe. Get well.

246
00:20:51,185 --> 00:20:53,687
You'll recover, okay?

247
00:20:53,687 --> 00:20:55,589
Of course.

248
00:20:57,573 --> 00:20:59,336
Don't cry.

249
00:21:03,914 --> 00:21:08,302
Make sure the public doesn't know.

250
00:21:08,302 --> 00:21:10,838
You know, for Savana.

251
00:21:10,838 --> 00:21:12,973
Noted, Ma'am.

252
00:21:16,155 --> 00:21:18,522
Uncle, get well soon.

253
00:21:27,252 --> 00:21:30,047
Nurse, how's my father?

254
00:21:30,047 --> 00:21:32,159
He's doing okay now, Ma'am.

255
00:21:32,159 --> 00:21:36,497
His lungs got affected by the substance.
That's why he needs oxygen.

256
00:21:36,497 --> 00:21:40,800
But he'll recover faster
if he won't take any drugs.

257
00:21:48,952 --> 00:21:53,514
Josh... We'll shoot the independent scenes
for now.

258
00:21:53,514 --> 00:21:55,758
We don't want to waste time.

259
00:21:55,758 --> 00:21:58,399
We'll shoot while Joyce isn't here...
while she's busy.

260
00:21:58,399 --> 00:22:00,221
Okay?

261
00:22:00,221 --> 00:22:01,489
No problem, Director Phil.

262
00:22:01,489 --> 00:22:04,224
Okay. Please retouch his makeup.

263
00:22:06,553 --> 00:22:08,854
Something bothering you, love?

264
00:22:10,693 --> 00:22:12,494
Nothing.

265
00:22:13,701 --> 00:22:18,505
I'm just wondering if the scenes
we will shoot today are enough.

266
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:25,468
You don't have to pretend that
you're not worried about Joyce.

267
00:22:30,986 --> 00:22:32,574
Love?

268
00:22:34,821 --> 00:22:37,089
It's normal.

269
00:22:38,011 --> 00:22:40,112
She's your actress.

270
00:22:40,831 --> 00:22:43,430
If you're concerned about the movie,

271
00:22:43,430 --> 00:22:47,233
you're also worried about
what your actors are going through.

272
00:22:49,136 --> 00:22:54,274
Yeah, but... I told her to keep us updated.

273
00:22:56,172 --> 00:22:58,040
Do you want to see her?

274
00:23:02,249 --> 00:23:03,817
I don't think I should.

275
00:23:03,817 --> 00:23:05,219
I'm also busy.

276
00:23:05,219 --> 00:23:07,220
We've got work to do.

277
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:15,261
We'll take care of everything here.

278
00:23:16,764 --> 00:23:18,598
Right, Borj?

279
00:23:20,714 --> 00:23:22,770
Yes, Boss Bro.

280
00:23:22,770 --> 00:23:27,907
You should go if Miss Joyce's father
is in a serious situation.

281
00:23:28,847 --> 00:23:30,966
We got this.

282
00:23:30,966 --> 00:23:34,682
If I can command the whole fashion week,

283
00:23:34,682 --> 00:23:35,849
I can do this.

284
00:23:35,849 --> 00:23:39,586
It's a small movie in a rustic little town.

285
00:23:40,788 --> 00:23:42,129
Hey.

286
00:23:42,974 --> 00:23:44,511
Go.

287
00:23:48,393 --> 00:23:50,563
Thank you, Love.

288
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:06,608
Are you just going to let him go, Miss?

289
00:24:11,209 --> 00:24:18,715
Men, like dogs,
should be let out once in a while.

290
00:24:21,062 --> 00:24:23,830
"Who let the dogs out" kind of drama.

291
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:29,503
I also want to make sure...

292
00:24:29,503 --> 00:24:32,338
if he still knows his way back home.

293
00:24:36,810 --> 00:24:38,372
Okay.

294
00:24:46,054 --> 00:24:47,427
Hey.

295
00:24:53,516 --> 00:24:55,106
How are you?

296
00:24:58,132 --> 00:25:00,867
Sorry, I was busy with work.

297
00:25:02,237 --> 00:25:08,075
The case I'm handling
became a bit complicated.

298
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:12,541
It was only neglect at first, Joyce,
but the case against Casa Fuerte

299
00:25:12,541 --> 00:25:15,382
has escalated into murder.

300
00:25:15,382 --> 00:25:18,018
Hans, it sounds serious.

301
00:25:18,018 --> 00:25:19,591
I know.

302
00:25:20,523 --> 00:25:23,992
I don't want to jump to conclusions, but...

303
00:25:26,727 --> 00:25:31,664
I can only think of one suspect
who would silence the victim.

304
00:25:33,473 --> 00:25:36,609
Do you think Casa Fuerte
has something to do with it?

305
00:25:39,403 --> 00:25:41,608
It's possible.

306
00:25:41,608 --> 00:25:49,288
So I'll get going, Joyce,
because I still have lots to do.

307
00:25:49,288 --> 00:25:52,624
I will have to check the investigation,
but...

308
00:25:53,991 --> 00:25:56,759
Honestly, Hans...

309
00:25:57,748 --> 00:26:00,884
Honestly, I feel embarrassed.

310
00:26:02,229 --> 00:26:06,767
Your work is important,
but you're here taking care of me.

311
00:26:06,767 --> 00:26:10,371
Joyce, I want to be here for you.

312
00:26:10,371 --> 00:26:12,172
I'm okay.

313
00:26:13,492 --> 00:26:15,994
My dad's okay too.

314
00:26:17,978 --> 00:26:19,630
Okay?

315
00:26:21,615 --> 00:26:23,884
So go do your work, please.

316
00:26:23,884 --> 00:26:26,352
I'm asking you.

317
00:26:28,288 --> 00:26:33,293
I'll be more focused,
knowing you're also focused on your work.

318
00:26:37,076 --> 00:26:38,618
Joyce.

319
00:26:39,566 --> 00:26:41,126
Thank you.

320
00:26:42,603 --> 00:26:44,671
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

321
00:26:44,671 --> 00:26:47,106
- Feel better, okay?
- Yeah.

322
00:27:00,756 --> 00:27:02,557
Liam.

323
00:27:03,672 --> 00:27:05,188
Attorney.

324
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:08,628
I have to go.

325
00:27:09,663 --> 00:27:11,998
- Call you later?
- Be safe.

326
00:27:31,018 --> 00:27:32,886
Liam.

327
00:27:32,886 --> 00:27:35,288
What are you doing here?

328
00:27:37,791 --> 00:27:40,360
I just want to know how your father is doing.

329
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:42,262
How is he?

330
00:27:45,207 --> 00:27:47,068
He's okay.

331
00:27:47,068 --> 00:27:49,369
My father's okay.

332
00:27:52,570 --> 00:27:54,872
Did you abandon the filming?

333
00:27:57,124 --> 00:28:01,381
Yeah. I told them I'll be right back.

334
00:28:05,151 --> 00:28:06,257
Excuse me.

335
00:28:06,257 --> 00:28:08,489
This is the call I'm waiting for
from the rehab.

336
00:28:08,489 --> 00:28:10,790
I need to take this.

337
00:28:12,860 --> 00:28:13,927
Hello?

338
00:28:13,927 --> 00:28:17,730
Joyce, your father is... asleep.

339
00:28:23,161 --> 00:28:25,066
Good evening.

340
00:28:43,557 --> 00:28:45,425
- Attorney...
- Madame...

341
00:28:49,029 --> 00:28:52,065
Are you going to move to another house?

342
00:28:52,065 --> 00:28:55,168
Let me know if you need help, okay?

343
00:28:55,168 --> 00:28:57,203
You can call me.

344
00:28:58,138 --> 00:29:00,741
My husband was right.

345
00:29:00,741 --> 00:29:03,977
We should have kept silent.

346
00:29:03,977 --> 00:29:09,382
If I wasn't stubborn,
my husband would still be alive.

347
00:29:12,152 --> 00:29:16,122
There's no justice for poor people like us.

348
00:29:17,107 --> 00:29:18,468
Hans.

349
00:29:23,497 --> 00:29:24,865
Excuse me.

350
00:29:24,865 --> 00:29:27,800
Let's talk later. I'll be right back, okay?

351
00:29:32,739 --> 00:29:34,640
Do you have leads?

352
00:29:35,576 --> 00:29:39,746
I owe you a lot for helping me
solve a lot of cases.

353
00:29:39,746 --> 00:29:42,849
I told you to apply as an NBI agent.

354
00:29:43,584 --> 00:29:46,419
Here. Look at this.

355
00:29:50,257 --> 00:29:54,595
This man was captured by the CCTV

356
00:29:54,595 --> 00:29:57,330
entering this alley
around the time of the murder.

357
00:30:02,970 --> 00:30:05,171
Can I have a copy of this?

358
00:30:07,307 --> 00:30:08,375
Sure.

359
00:30:08,375 --> 00:30:11,944
But it's just going to be
between the two of us.

360
00:30:18,885 --> 00:30:21,088
Closer to each other.

361
00:30:21,088 --> 00:30:22,422
A little bit. There.

362
00:30:22,422 --> 00:30:25,258
We're going to do this in one take, okay?

363
00:30:25,258 --> 00:30:27,127
- Miss Via.
- Quiet, everyone.

364
00:30:27,127 --> 00:30:28,562
- Miss Via...
- Quiet on the set!

365
00:30:28,562 --> 00:30:33,233
Sir Liam's next movie
should be based on your life.

366
00:30:33,233 --> 00:30:35,235
I already have a title for it.

367
00:30:35,235 --> 00:30:39,672
"Love: The Murder of a Martyred Heart".

368
00:30:39,672 --> 00:30:41,274
That's a massacre film.

369
00:30:41,274 --> 00:30:43,476
I'd watch that movie.

370
00:30:44,311 --> 00:30:45,746
My gosh, Miss Via.

371
00:30:45,746 --> 00:30:47,914
Why are we even here?

372
00:30:47,914 --> 00:30:52,285
No hot water, no nightlife, no boys!

373
00:30:52,285 --> 00:30:54,788
It's going to kill me.

374
00:30:54,788 --> 00:30:58,425
Queenie, for an assistant...

375
00:30:58,425 --> 00:31:01,995
you sure do talk a lot, don't you?

376
00:31:01,995 --> 00:31:03,597
I know, right?

377
00:31:03,597 --> 00:31:05,321
But Miss Via,

378
00:31:05,321 --> 00:31:09,435
I'm just verbalizing the feelings
you're bottling up inside.

379
00:31:10,566 --> 00:31:16,777
Do you think I'm happy seeing my boyfriend

380
00:31:16,777 --> 00:31:20,814
fulfill his dreams with someone else?

381
00:31:20,814 --> 00:31:24,484
Especially with another woman?

382
00:31:24,484 --> 00:31:26,171
What happened, Miss Via?

383
00:31:26,171 --> 00:31:31,324
I mean, Sir Liam used to cling to you
like a snake.

384
00:31:31,324 --> 00:31:35,795
But now, you're dealing with
a different kind of snake.

385
00:31:36,863 --> 00:31:41,168
Hey, Miss Via, I hope you didn't
get offended by what I said.

386
00:31:41,168 --> 00:31:43,236
I should go.

387
00:31:43,236 --> 00:31:44,471
No.

388
00:31:44,471 --> 00:31:45,972
You stay here.

389
00:31:45,972 --> 00:31:48,341
We still have work to do.

390
00:31:48,341 --> 00:31:49,975
I'm going to leave.

391
00:31:49,975 --> 00:31:52,181
I'll be working from home.

392
00:31:52,913 --> 00:31:54,549
That's unfair, Miss Via.

393
00:31:54,549 --> 00:31:59,386
Please don't leave me
in the company of mosquitoes and crickets.

394
00:31:59,386 --> 00:32:00,887
I already told you.

395
00:32:00,887 --> 00:32:04,440
Liam is the only reason I'm here.

396
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:07,059
But he is not here anymore.

397
00:32:07,894 --> 00:32:09,596
You can do it.

398
00:32:09,596 --> 00:32:10,664
Okay?

399
00:32:10,664 --> 00:32:12,133
Miss...

400
00:32:13,166 --> 00:32:16,402
I'll give you a raise
when we get back to Manila.

401
00:32:17,838 --> 00:32:21,374
Okay, back to work!

402
00:32:26,344 --> 00:32:29,015
Looks like you're in a hurry, Via.
Where are you off to?

403
00:32:29,015 --> 00:32:30,350
I'll go ahead, Mayor.

404
00:32:30,350 --> 00:32:31,518
- What?
- But...

405
00:32:31,518 --> 00:32:33,754
- There is something you should know.
- What is it?

406
00:32:33,754 --> 00:32:35,722
My assistant was telling me something.

407
00:32:35,722 --> 00:32:40,360
- What is it?
- She said your town needs more pizza places.

408
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,883
What?

409
00:32:41,883 --> 00:32:44,264
That's not true.

410
00:32:44,264 --> 00:32:45,732
I'll get going.

411
00:32:47,499 --> 00:32:52,105
You know what to do until I get back, okay?

412
00:32:54,107 --> 00:32:55,282
Yes.

413
00:32:55,282 --> 00:32:57,677
Keep an eye on Liam.

414
00:32:59,621 --> 00:33:02,449
I feel so good to be
surrounded by loyal friends.

415
00:33:02,449 --> 00:33:03,884
I know.

416
00:33:03,884 --> 00:33:05,819
Anything for you, Via.

417
00:33:05,819 --> 00:33:10,490
Remember that I'm counting on you
and your family's support

418
00:33:10,490 --> 00:33:11,658
in the next elections.

419
00:33:11,658 --> 00:33:12,759
Come on.

420
00:33:12,759 --> 00:33:15,462
- When did we ever fail you?
- I know.

421
00:33:15,462 --> 00:33:18,999
Wow. The beauty of conditional love.

422
00:33:18,999 --> 00:33:22,435
- That's true.
- It's not too complicated.

423
00:33:22,435 --> 00:33:24,470
- Okay. I'll go ahead.
- Bye.

424
00:33:30,477 --> 00:33:32,445
Hello, Light of Hope?

425
00:33:33,313 --> 00:33:36,448
I had Joyce see a feng shui expert.

426
00:33:36,448 --> 00:33:41,253
I had her wear bracelets and amulets.

427
00:33:41,253 --> 00:33:43,322
She's actually complaining about it.

428
00:33:43,322 --> 00:33:48,860
She said she's not a dog
or an animal to wear a collar.

429
00:33:50,986 --> 00:33:54,790
We even lit candles in church.

430
00:33:55,719 --> 00:33:58,103
You know how showbiz works, right?

431
00:33:58,103 --> 00:34:03,242
Beauty and talent
are not enough to make you famous.

432
00:34:03,242 --> 00:34:05,744
You also need luck.

433
00:34:06,745 --> 00:34:10,148
Looks like I need to
arrange a divination for her.

434
00:34:11,450 --> 00:34:12,918
Why?

435
00:34:12,918 --> 00:34:16,021
Recently, I've noticed...

436
00:34:16,021 --> 00:34:20,258
our amulets no longer work against bad luck.

437
00:34:22,328 --> 00:34:25,797
Ever since... you came.

438
00:34:29,243 --> 00:34:31,564
Let me get this straight with you.

439
00:34:33,284 --> 00:34:36,520
What are your plans for my daughter's career?

440
00:34:39,678 --> 00:34:42,481
To make it clearer...

441
00:34:42,481 --> 00:34:45,016
what's your plan with my daughter?

442
00:34:47,286 --> 00:34:51,490
Joyce and I are just doing
a side project, Auntie.

443
00:34:51,490 --> 00:34:58,196
I'm not stopping her from
taking on other responsibilities.

444
00:34:59,298 --> 00:35:03,601
And based on what I see, she looks happy.

445
00:35:05,170 --> 00:35:08,372
She's happy now because she has money.

446
00:35:08,372 --> 00:35:10,875
But what if it runs out?

447
00:35:10,875 --> 00:35:13,810
Do you think she will still be happy?

448
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:17,114
Auntie.

449
00:35:17,114 --> 00:35:20,817
I'm sure Joyce knows what she's doing.

450
00:35:21,753 --> 00:35:26,958
And you also know what I'm doing as a mother.

451
00:35:27,813 --> 00:35:30,661
I'm just protecting her.

452
00:35:30,661 --> 00:35:33,963
If she gives up on her ambition,

453
00:35:33,963 --> 00:35:37,199
I don't have anyone else to blame but you.

454
00:35:41,839 --> 00:35:43,141
Everything's set, Mom.

455
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,910
The wellness center
is already waiting for dad.

456
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:49,247
You take care of your father.

457
00:35:49,247 --> 00:35:52,950
I'm tired
of cleaning up your mess and your father's.

458
00:35:55,320 --> 00:35:57,155
You know the drill.

459
00:35:57,155 --> 00:36:00,591
Make sure no one recognizes you.

460
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:04,429
Go there later tonight.

461
00:36:19,067 --> 00:36:22,261
[Pares With Love]
Their food is the best.

462
00:36:22,262 --> 00:36:25,398
It really is good, Sir Edmond.

463
00:36:25,400 --> 00:36:27,218
Just call me Uncle Edmond.

464
00:36:27,218 --> 00:36:32,289
And sorry for interrupting your work.

465
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:34,730
And also you, Liam.

466
00:36:34,730 --> 00:36:38,463
You had to fly here to Paris.

467
00:36:38,463 --> 00:36:39,898
Sorry?

468
00:36:39,898 --> 00:36:41,466
Paris?

469
00:36:41,466 --> 00:36:43,401
Here.

470
00:36:43,401 --> 00:36:44,669
Paris.

471
00:36:44,669 --> 00:36:46,580
It's a store that sells braised beef stew.

472
00:36:47,197 --> 00:36:49,807
When Joyce was still a kid,

473
00:36:49,807 --> 00:36:52,933
she used to cry

474
00:36:52,934 --> 00:36:57,466
whenever I would leave and be gone
for a long time.

475
00:36:57,467 --> 00:36:59,950
So to make her stop crying...

476
00:37:00,652 --> 00:37:04,856
I would tell her about Paris.

477
00:37:04,856 --> 00:37:08,726
I used to tell her I'd go back there
because it was beautiful.

478
00:37:08,726 --> 00:37:14,198
So she grew up dreaming of seeing Paris.

479
00:37:16,501 --> 00:37:23,007
She didn't know
that I was referring to this place.

480
00:37:23,007 --> 00:37:24,844
My Paris.

481
00:37:26,940 --> 00:37:31,977
And that's where I'm going to check-in.

482
00:37:33,801 --> 00:37:35,634
[Light of Hope Rehabilitation Center]

483
00:38:38,416 --> 00:38:44,689
<i>Do you think I'm happy
seeing my boyfriend fulfill his dreams</i>

484
00:38:44,689 --> 00:38:48,793
<i>with someone else?</i>

485
00:38:48,793 --> 00:38:51,596
<i>Especially with another woman?</i>

486
00:38:51,596 --> 00:38:53,298
What happened, Miss Via?

487
00:38:53,298 --> 00:38:58,836
I mean,
Sir Liam used to cling to you like a snake.

488
00:39:05,376 --> 00:39:06,611
Dad.

489
00:39:06,611 --> 00:39:08,812
What are you doing here?

490
00:39:10,114 --> 00:39:15,082
Am I not allowed to visit my only daughter?

491
00:39:15,082 --> 00:39:18,122
My knee is acting up again.

492
00:39:18,122 --> 00:39:19,835
I need you to massage it.

493
00:39:26,964 --> 00:39:28,476
What is this?

494
00:39:37,141 --> 00:39:38,624
Okay.

495
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:42,804
I'll stay in Paris for now.

496
00:39:47,186 --> 00:39:49,821
Dear, I'm sorry.

497
00:39:49,821 --> 00:39:51,889
Your father is weak.

498
00:39:52,657 --> 00:39:55,659
I wasn't able to fulfill my promise again.

499
00:40:00,832 --> 00:40:04,168
We can get through this, Dad.

500
00:40:07,605 --> 00:40:10,307
I'm not mad at you, okay?

501
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:14,406
I will never get mad at you.

502
00:40:19,684 --> 00:40:21,265
Bye.

503
00:40:24,622 --> 00:40:27,491
I love you so much, Dad.

504
00:40:29,560 --> 00:40:33,063
I'll wait for you to get out.
I'll be right here.

505
00:40:35,733 --> 00:40:37,869
I love you.

506
00:40:37,869 --> 00:40:39,710
Goodbye.

507
00:41:06,564 --> 00:41:08,599
I can explain that.

508
00:41:10,668 --> 00:41:14,005
Do you still have to do that?

509
00:41:14,005 --> 00:41:15,473
- Ouch!
- Sorry.

510
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:17,274
Careful!

511
00:41:20,011 --> 00:41:21,579
But...

512
00:41:21,579 --> 00:41:24,548
Liam is just helping Joyce.

513
00:41:25,583 --> 00:41:27,952
Dad, just trust me.

514
00:41:27,952 --> 00:41:30,755
Joyce is his actress.

515
00:41:30,755 --> 00:41:33,824
He's just protecting her.

516
00:41:47,438 --> 00:41:51,776
Only one of us believes that lie.

517
00:41:51,776 --> 00:41:53,810
And that's not me.

518
00:41:57,815 --> 00:41:59,484
You had them followed?

519
00:41:59,484 --> 00:42:04,755
Clearly, you're doubting your boyfriend.

520
00:42:05,568 --> 00:42:08,178
But I don't have concrete evidence.

521
00:42:09,994 --> 00:42:12,929
I still trust Liam, Dad.

522
00:42:14,402 --> 00:42:16,370
He's still mine.

523
00:42:19,971 --> 00:42:23,140
The lies we tell ourselves.

524
00:42:23,908 --> 00:42:29,146
Well, you need to convince yourself.

525
00:42:29,914 --> 00:42:33,017
You even risked your life for him.

526
00:42:33,017 --> 00:42:35,352
You don't know anything.

527
00:42:36,153 --> 00:42:38,789
Liam and I love each other.

528
00:42:43,661 --> 00:42:45,495
Via!

529
00:42:46,998 --> 00:42:49,866
I didn't raise you to become stupid.

530
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:54,272
I can control the world
in the palm of my hands,

531
00:42:54,272 --> 00:43:00,711
but I have a daughter
who's being manipulated by a man.

532
00:43:00,711 --> 00:43:04,882
I can fix my problems on my own, Dad.

533
00:43:04,882 --> 00:43:06,717
Make sure you can.

534
00:43:06,717 --> 00:43:08,585
Because if not...

535
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:12,756
I will be the one to solve them, Via.

536
00:43:39,283 --> 00:43:41,285
Before we start...

537
00:43:41,285 --> 00:43:46,757
who would like to recite the Serenity prayer?

538
00:43:48,137 --> 00:43:49,994
Edmond, welcome back.

539
00:43:49,994 --> 00:43:51,795
Go ahead.

540
00:43:54,690 --> 00:43:56,691
Heavenly Father...

541
00:43:57,735 --> 00:44:00,504
Grant unto us the serenity of mind

542
00:44:00,504 --> 00:44:04,074
to accept that which cannot be changed.

543
00:44:05,009 --> 00:44:09,546
Give us the courage to change
the things we can.

544
00:44:10,748 --> 00:44:13,484
Living one day at a time,

545
00:44:13,484 --> 00:44:17,088
enjoying the moment one at a time,

546
00:44:17,088 --> 00:44:20,791
trusting that you will make all things right

547
00:44:20,791 --> 00:44:23,894
if I surrender to your will.

548
00:44:26,130 --> 00:44:28,265
Who will start?

549
00:44:30,229 --> 00:44:31,830
Okay, Edmond.

550
00:44:35,806 --> 00:44:37,441
My name's Edmond.

551
00:44:37,441 --> 00:44:39,496
Edmond Trinidad.

552
00:44:41,348 --> 00:44:44,651
This is my fourth time coming here.

553
00:44:45,349 --> 00:44:50,121
Because no matter how hard I try,

554
00:44:50,121 --> 00:44:57,128
I can't help but escape reality

555
00:44:57,128 --> 00:45:03,200
whenever I remember
the horrible things I experienced in the past.

556
00:45:04,969 --> 00:45:09,099
I've broken my promise to my daughter
a lot of times...

557
00:45:09,100 --> 00:45:11,809
That I'll get my life fixed.

558
00:45:11,809 --> 00:45:15,800
But what you're doing is a good step, Edmond.

559
00:45:15,801 --> 00:45:21,652
You said
you want to escape something from your past.

560
00:45:21,652 --> 00:45:23,744
It's not easy.

561
00:45:23,745 --> 00:45:28,859
But maybe the real solution is
to deal with it.

562
00:45:30,448 --> 00:45:35,266
You only need a strong support system
from your family.

563
00:45:35,266 --> 00:45:37,266
We, here in the wellness center,

564
00:45:37,267 --> 00:45:38,367
can help you

565
00:45:38,367 --> 00:45:43,373
if you want to talk
about what's bothering you.

566
00:45:43,374 --> 00:45:48,971
Free yourself from your horrible past.

567
00:45:48,972 --> 00:45:50,974
Can you do that?

568
00:45:54,685 --> 00:45:56,259
I can.

569
00:45:57,354 --> 00:46:01,525
<i>I don't care if you're innocent.</i>

570
00:46:01,525 --> 00:46:05,029
You're all the same to me.

571
00:46:05,029 --> 00:46:10,434
You will say you took the money,
because you're going to jail anyway.

572
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:11,736
Where is it?

573
00:46:11,736 --> 00:46:14,705
It's gone!

574
00:46:14,705 --> 00:46:16,747
<i>It's me!</i>

575
00:46:16,747 --> 00:46:18,542
<i>I took the money!</i>

576
00:46:18,542 --> 00:46:19,944
I used it!

577
00:46:19,944 --> 00:46:21,845
It's all gone!

578
00:46:23,214 --> 00:46:24,215
See?

579
00:46:24,215 --> 00:46:26,583
Finally, you admit.

580
00:46:29,386 --> 00:46:33,557
I only want someone who will take the blame

581
00:46:33,557 --> 00:46:37,761
so that the senators who don't like me
will stop bothering me.

582
00:46:38,562 --> 00:46:42,074
<i>That's what you're going to tell the police.</i>

583
00:46:48,272 --> 00:46:50,307
Go get him.

584
00:46:50,307 --> 00:46:53,777
Drag him out of here.
He won't change his statement now.

585
00:47:10,824 --> 00:47:12,625
Uncle Ramon?

586
00:47:15,299 --> 00:47:19,903
Big bro, here's your dessert.

587
00:47:23,274 --> 00:47:25,942
It's not Uncle Ramon's birthday.

588
00:47:50,273 --> 00:47:51,882
What's that?

589
00:48:05,280 --> 00:48:08,063
Where's Uncle Edmond? Can I talk to him?

590
00:48:08,063 --> 00:48:10,321
It will make my investigation easier.

591
00:48:10,321 --> 00:48:12,623
Liam left a lot of debts in Casa Fuerte.

592
00:48:12,623 --> 00:48:13,844
Dad told me about it.

593
00:48:13,844 --> 00:48:15,392
That's why Dad is paying for it now.

594
00:48:15,392 --> 00:48:18,852
Make sure you stay with Via
because if you don't, you'll be dead.

595
00:48:18,852 --> 00:48:20,156
What else do I have to do, Liam?

596
00:48:20,156 --> 00:48:22,933
I know that you know we have a problem, Liam.

597
00:48:22,933 --> 00:48:24,172
Can you tell me the truth?

598
00:48:24,172 --> 00:48:27,471
Are you just staying with me
because you know that if we break up,

599
00:48:27,471 --> 00:48:28,930
my dad might do something to you?

600
00:48:28,930 --> 00:48:31,735
I don't know anymore!
I don't know! I'm getting confused!

601
00:48:31,735 --> 00:48:33,177
I just want to explode!

602
00:48:33,177 --> 00:48:36,190
If he fights me,
he's not the one who will get hurt.

603
00:48:36,190 --> 00:48:38,949
It's the people who matter to him.

604
00:48:38,949 --> 00:48:43,620
I'm sorry
for dragging you into my miserable life.
